{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfs3oweSkSVWTu5yrS6J5","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The age-fallback change is in place: `AgeFallback` enum, the `age_fallback` parameter, the pinned-constraint bypass, and multi-version mode using `NEWEST`. The two requested test files pass (66 tests), and `test_resolver.py` also passes (99 across all three). Nothing is committed.\n\n**What changed**\n\n- **`src/fromager/resolver.py`**\n  - New `AgeFallback` enum (`ALL`, `NEWEST`, `NONE`) with a class docstring.\n  - `find_all_matching_from_provider()` takes `age_fallback: AgeFallback = AgeFallback.ALL` in place of the boolean. The three fallback branches log the exact messages you specified.\n  - If `provider.constraints` holds a single `==` constraint for the requirement, the age filter is skipped and the INFO message is logged. The check reuses the existing `_has_equality_pin` helper, so a wildcard pin such as `==1.*` is still age-filtered.\n  - Docstrings are updated.\n- **`src/fromager/bootstrap_requirement_resolver.py`**: passes `resolver.AgeFallback.NEWEST` when `multiple_versions` is set and `ALL` otherwise, with a short comment explaining why.\n- **`tests/test_cooldown.py`**\n  - The old `fallback_on_empty_age_filter=False` test is now `..._with_none_fallback` and uses `AgeFallback.NONE`.\n  - New tests cover NEWEST fallback, a parametrized exact-pin test over all three fallbacks, and a range constraint (`<2.0.0`) that is still age-filtered.\n- **`tests/test_bootstrap_requirement_resolver.py`**\n  - A parametrized test checks which fallback each mode passes.\n  - An end-to-end test with a mocked index: in multi-version mode, a package whose releases are all outside the window resolves to its newest version.\n  - A pinned-but-old version resolves in both modes.\n\n**Things to know**\n\n- In multi-version mode the cache-server fallback in `_resolve_and_extend` now runs only when the provider returns nothing at all. The NEWEST path returns a result whenever any candidate exists, so the cache lookup is rarely reached. This follows from the spec, but it is a behaviour change.\n- `ruff format` and `ruff check` pass on the four changed files. `mypy` is not installed for the project environment, so the type check did not run.\n- I did not add a Sphinx `versionadded` note because I didn't determine the last git tag. The docs contain no references to the age-window behaviour, so I didn't change any."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2502,"cache_read_input_tokens":126160,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2502},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"8e69fa9a-75ee-4abb-882a-eba058cff68b","uuid":"eb41f3a0-88e8-4808-932e-91021277e177","timestamp":"2026-10-09T17:22:04.604Z","request_id":"req_011Cfs3owAuyhrxN6ydAqDF7"}
